From d3c517cca50481a0b1b9b0fcaa8795bb7d3a6b8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:14:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): the program sim, setup sheet, tool list and cutting
 data know a tool-less wire cut

A Wire Contour mounts no library tool (#532), so its Operation::tool is
the empty word. Each reader now asks KindInfo::mounts_tool():

- program stock sim: plan_program leaves the wire cut out of the plan
  (like the probe and torch), and simulate_document refuses the verdict
  by name ("a wire cut is verified by the wire laws, not the stock
  sim") instead of "tool  is not in the library"
- setup sheet: the TOOL cell is "cond <id>", with the condition, wire
  diameter and gap the machine states under the row; no missing-tool line
- tool list and export: no row for the empty tool
- cutting data: refuses by name that a wire cut mounts no library tool

A milling op whose tool is gone is refused or listed exactly as before.
Pinned by crates/app/tests/wire_readers.rs.

Fixes #1110

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
